# HQS inspection letter intake

Landlords text a housing-authority fail letter (PDF or photo) to the Ulo number. Ulo classifies the attachment, extracts deficiencies, confirms with the landlord, then creates one `inspection_reports` row + owner-responsibility work orders.

## Surfaces

| Concern | Where |
|---|---|
| Schema | `inspection_reports`, `inspection_source_documents`, `hqs_owner_tenant_unit_map`, `hqs_fail_category_trade_map`, `maintenance_requests.inspection_report_id` |
| Pure extract | `shared/maintenance/hqsInspectionLetter.ts` |
| PDF vs photo routes | `shared/maintenance/hqsLetterMediaExtract.ts` — PDF = text; photo = **vision OCR** (not rehost-only) |
| Confirm + create | `supabase/functions/_shared/sms/hqsInspectionLetterConfirm.ts` |
| SMS YES/unit replies | `hqs_unit_reply` / `hqs_confirm` in inbound registry |
| Landlord can't-process | `landlordInboundCantProcess.ts` — link-only / unsupported type / unrecognized attachment (landlord only) |
| Property Intelligence | Smart Inspection Report panel lists HQS letters via `listHqsInspectionReportsForBuilding` |

## Rules

- Do not create `inspection_reports` or work orders until landlord replies **YES**
- No unit mapping → ask which unit; store `(owner_id, tenant_id) → unit_id`; auto-resolve later letters
- Emergency section may be absent — never require an Emergency header
- `is_abated` → separate `inspection.hap_abatement` graph event + Needs Attention alert
- Emergency rows → urgent/habitability alert tier (same path as gas/fire/flooding)
- Standard due date = reinspection date if stated, else inspection date + 30 days
- Fail category → vendor trade via `hqs_fail_category_trade_map` / `mapHqsFailCategoryToVendorTrade`
- Email ingest does **not** exist yet — MMS (+ dashboard Smart Inspection Report) only
- Landlord **link-only** (ViewLetter / habc / HQS) → ask for photo or PDF; never fetch or classify a bare URL
- Landlord **unsupported** attachment (HEIC, video, office docs) → name the type; ask for JPEG/PNG/PDF
- Landlord **unrecognized** supported file → say we support HQS letters; offer HELP → human (not maintenance fallback)
- These three replies are **not** tenant_distress; distress still applies independently if they react badly

## Do not

- Assume every letter has an Emergency (24-hr) section
- Create tickets before YES
- Treat photo MMS as rehost-only — must run vision OCR for HQS classification
- Open or classify bare links
- Fire can't-process replies for tenants or vendors
